From: INMYS <support@inmys.ru>
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: mux: pca954x: add PCA9540B support

The PCA9540B is a 2-channel I2C multiplexer in an 8-pin package with a
fixed address of 0x70.  Its control register is the same as the one of
the PCA9544: bits 1:0 select the channel (binary) and bit 2 is an enable
bit that has to be set, otherwise the part stays disconnected and nothing
behind the mux answers.

The Linux driver has had this entry for years (pca_9540 in
drivers/i2c/muxes/i2c-mux-pca954x.c: nchans = 2, enable = 0x4,
muxtype = pca954x_ismux), but U-Boot's copy of the driver is missing it,
so a `nxp,pca9540` node in the device tree is silently ignored.

The INMYS NMS-SM-K1892VM21YA module uses a PCA9540BGD (D30) to split the
SoC I2C2 into the I2C_INT (3.3 V) and I2C_INT_1V8 branches.

Signed-off-by: INMYS <support@inmys.ru>
---
 drivers/i2c/muxes/pca954x.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/muxes/pca954x.c b/drivers/i2c/muxes/pca954x.c
--- a/drivers/i2c/muxes/pca954x.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/muxes/pca954x.c
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 DECLARE_GLOBAL_DATA_PTR;
 
 enum pca_type {
+	PCA9540,
 	PCA9543,
 	PCA9544,
 	PCA9546,
@@ -45,6 +46,11 @@ struct pca954x_priv {
 };
 
 static const struct chip_desc chips[] = {
+	[PCA9540] = {
+		.enable = 0x4,
+		.muxtype = pca954x_ismux,
+		.width = 2,
+	},
 	[PCA9543] = {
 		.muxtype = pca954x_isswi,
 		.width = 2,
@@ -106,6 +112,7 @@ static const struct i2c_mux_ops pca954x_ops = {
 };
 
 static const struct udevice_id pca954x_ids[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "nxp,pca9540", .data = PCA9540 },
 	{ .compatible = "nxp,pca9543", .data = PCA9543 },
 	{ .compatible = "nxp,pca9544", .data = PCA9544 },
 	{ .compatible = "nxp,pca9546", .data = PCA9546 },
-- 
